<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Nothing this app stores may leave the device.

   The whole dataset is credentials and a record of the user's life: two API keys
   in plaintext (`voice_prefs`), the vault (`vault_prefs` — logins and card
   numbers), the notebook, meeting transcripts under files/meetings/, and, in
   grounding mode, screenshots of whatever was on screen. There is no
   non-sensitive remainder worth carrying to a new device: the endpoints have
   compiled-in defaults, and `device_id` *should* be regenerated per device,
   because two bodies registering the same id with one hub is a bug.

   `android:allowBackup="false"` is the other half of this and does not replace
   it: on Android 12+ it stops cloud backup but leaves **device-to-device
   transfer** permitted, which is what <device-transfer> below is for. Both are
   set so that flipping one back on does not silently re-enable the other.

   The vault would not survive a restore anyway — its key lives in the hardware
   Keystore and does not travel — but an undecryptable blob arriving on a new
   device is pure downside, not a safeguard.

   `device_root` is a documented domain for these rules — "like root but for
   device-protected storage", per the Auto Backup reference. AGP 8.3's
   `FullBackupContent` lint check still validates against the older
   `full-backup-content` domain list, which predates `device_*`, and reports it
   as an error; because `lintVitalRelease` runs on every release build, that
   false positive is what used to make `assembleRelease` fail outright. The
   ignores below are scoped to those two lines and nothing else.
-->
<data-extraction-rules xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." tools:ignore="FullBackupContent" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." tools:ignore="FullBackupContent" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
